---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const title = 'Privacy Policy – Globle Unlimited';
const description =
  'How Globle Unlimited handles your data: local browser storage, analytics, advertising cookies, your GDPR/CCPA rights, and children’s privacy.';

const schema: Record<string, unknown>[] = [
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebPage', name: title, url: SITE.url + '/privacy-policy' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/privacy-policy" schema={schema}>
  <article class="prose legal">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › Privacy Policy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated mono">Last updated: {SITE.legalUpdated}</p>

    <p class="lede">
      This Privacy Policy explains what information {SITE.name} ({SITE.domain}, &ldquo;we&rdquo;,
      &ldquo;us&rdquo;) collects when you use our website and games, how we use it, and the choices
      you have. We keep data collection to a minimum: the game runs in your browser and does not
      require an account.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information stored in your browser</h3>
    <p>
      Globle Unlimited saves your game progress — including your guesses, streaks, best scores and
      daily completion status — in your browser&rsquo;s <strong>local storage</strong>. This data
      lives on your device only. We do not transmit it to our servers, and we cannot read it. You
      can clear it at any time through your browser settings.
    </p>
    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p>
      Like most websites, our hosting and analytics providers automatically receive certain
      technical information when you visit, such as your IP address, browser type, device type,
      referring page, and the pages you view. This information is used to operate the site, keep it
      secure, and understand aggregate usage. We do not use it to personally identify you.
    </p>
    <h3>Information you send us</h3>
    <p>
      If you email us or use our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, we receive the information you
      choose to share (such as your email address and message) so we can respond. We use it only
      for that purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      A cookie is a small file stored on your device. We and our service providers use cookies and
      similar technologies (including local storage) for these purposes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Essential:</strong> to make the game function and remember your progress.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> to understand, in aggregate, how the site is used so we can
        improve it.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising:</strong> if and when we display ads, to serve and measure them (see
        the next section).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings. Blocking some cookies may
      affect how the site works.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      We may display advertising on this site, including through <strong>Google AdSense</strong>.
      When ads are enabled, third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies to serve ads
      based on your prior visits to this and other websites.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google&rsquo;s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you
        based on your visit to our site and/or other sites on the Internet.</li>
      <li>You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
      <li>You can opt out of some third-party vendors&rsquo; use of cookies for personalised
        advertising at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info/choices</a>
        or
        <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For more information about how Google uses data when you use our site, see
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google&rsquo;s privacy &amp; terms</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to measure traffic and understand how the site is
      used. Google Analytics sets cookies and collects information such as the pages you visit,
      your approximate location (derived from your IP address), your device and browser type, and
      how you arrived at the site. We use this data in aggregate to see which pages are popular and
      how the site performs. You can learn how Google uses this data at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google&rsquo;s privacy &amp; terms</a>
      and opt out with the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide, operate and maintain the game and website.</li>
      <li>To improve gameplay, content and performance.</li>
      <li>To respond to your messages and support requests.</li>
      <li>To display and measure advertising, where applicable.</li>
      <li>To keep the site secure and prevent abuse.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Legal bases (EEA/UK users)</h2>
    <p>
      Where the GDPR applies, we process data on the following bases: our <strong>legitimate
      interests</strong> in operating and improving the site; your <strong>consent</strong> for
      non-essential cookies and personalised advertising; and compliance with
      <strong>legal obligations</strong>. You may withdraw consent at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights and choices</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict
      the processing of your personal data, to object to processing, and to data portability.
      Residents of the EEA/UK have these rights under the GDPR; California residents have rights
      under the CCPA/CPRA, including the right to know, delete, and opt out of the &ldquo;sale&rdquo;
      or &ldquo;sharing&rdquo; of personal information. We do not sell personal information for
      money. To exercise any right, email us at
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Children&rsquo;s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our site is intended for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13. We do
      not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13 (or the equivalent minimum
      age in your jurisdiction). When ads are served, we configure them appropriately for a general
      audience. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us
      and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      Game progress remains in your browser until you clear it. Server logs and aggregate analytics
      are retained only as long as needed for the purposes described above. Messages you send us are
      kept as long as necessary to handle your request.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Data security</h2>
    <p>
      We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect information, including
      serving the site over HTTPS. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we
      cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
      Our site links to third-party websites (for example, our data sources and advertising
      partners). We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those sites. We encourage you
      to read their privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>12. International visitors</h2>
    <p>
      We operate online and may process information in countries other than your own. By using the
      site, you understand that your information may be processed in those locations.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Managing cookies in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      Most browsers let you view, block, and delete cookies through their settings. You can usually
      find these controls under &ldquo;Privacy&rdquo; or &ldquo;Cookies&rdquo; in Chrome, Firefox,
      Safari, or Edge. You can also browse in a private/incognito window, which clears cookies and
      local storage when you close it. Because Globle Unlimited stores your game progress in local
      storage, clearing site data will reset your streaks and stats.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>
      Some browsers offer a &ldquo;Do Not Track&rdquo; (DNT) signal. There is no industry-wide
      standard for how sites should respond to DNT, so we do not currently respond to DNT signals.
      You can still control advertising cookies using the opt-out tools listed in the Advertising
      section above.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Aggregated and de-identified data</h2>
    <p>
      We may create aggregated or de-identified data from usage information (for example, total
      visits or popular pages). This data does not identify you, and we may use and share it for
      analytics, reporting, and improving the Service. We will not attempt to re-identify such data.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the
      &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date above. Significant changes will be reflected on this page.
    </p>

    <h2>17. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or visit our
      <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal { padding-block: var(--space-12); }
  .crumb { font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--text-mute); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .crumb a { color: var(--text-dim); }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h1); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .updated { color: var(--text-mute); font-size: var(--fs-small); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .legal h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text); margin-top: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .legal ul { color: var(--text-dim); margin: var(--space-4) 0; padding-left: var(--space-6); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
